  [PASS] 46a THE RESULT, and it is a LIABILITY: the framework over-predicts the rotation of every one of the six tidal dwarfs, on both footings, with the external-field effect included.  The LambdaCDM expectation -- that a TDG is dark-matter free and obeys plain Newtonian gravity with its observed baryons -- fits them, and the framework does not   (canonical + EFE: mean +1.72 sigma per TDG, combined +4.21 sigma, chi^2 18.9/6; alt + EFE: +1.89 / +4.63 sigma; Newtonian: -0.26 / -0.63 sigma, chi^2 1.1/6)
  [PASS] 46b the framework's own a_0 footings make the tension SMALLER than the a_0 = 1.30e-10 that Lelli+2015 used, because a lower a_0 predicts lower velocities -- so part of the published 'MOND fails on TDGs' result is an a_0 choice, and that part is quantified here rather than left implicit.  It is not enough to remove the liability   (combined tension +4.96 sigma at a_0 = 1.30e-10 (the paper's value), +4.21 sigma at 9.36e-11 (canonical), +4.63 sigma at 1.13e-10 (alt))

